From 2117477071d40c413ee8e4154cba9b3c84268931 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:02:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/23] vk: decode feature and property structs of unsupported
 extensions

Guest encoders that were generated against the whole Vulkan registry,
such as the one in the API 34 system images, encode every struct they
know in the pNext chains of vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2(),
vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2() and vkCreateDevice(). The host only
has marshaling code for the extensions gfxstream supports, while
goldfish_vk_extension_structs knows the size of every struct. A guest
that chains, for example, VkPhysicalDeviceAccelerationStructure-
PropertiesKHR therefore passes the size lookup and then reaches the
default case of reservedunmarshal_extension_struct(), which aborts the
emulator:

  reservedunmarshal_extension_struct, Unhandled Vulkan structure type
  VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_PROPERTIES_KHR
  [1000150014], aborting.

Arknights: Endfield (Unity, Vulkan only) chains that struct into
vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2() right after creating its instance, so
it cannot start at all. The stream carries no length for
a struct, so the decoder cannot skip one it does not know.

Every struct that extends VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 or
VkPhysicalDeviceProperties2 is plain data. Add a table, generated from
vk.xml by scripts/gen-query-only-structs.py, with the C layout of each
such struct that has no generated case: 255 structs at
VK_HEADER_VERSION 350. The generated switches fall back to it in their
default cases:

- reservedunmarshal, marshal and unmarshal handle sType, the pNext
  chain and then the fields in order, the way the generated functions
  do (raw bytes, size_t as a big-endian 64-bit value);
- deepcopy copies the bytes and then the chain;
- transform has nothing to do and keeps walking the chain;
- the two size functions return the struct size instead of aborting,
  which also covers VK_KHR_ray_tracing_pipeline, whose structs had no
  size entry.

Guests cannot enable these extensions, so the structs must not reach
the driver either: the NVIDIA driver, for one, would report ray
tracing as supported. vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2() and
vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2() unlink them for the driver call and
put them back zeroed, which is what a device without the extensions
reports, and vkCreateDevice() drops them from its copy of the create
info. Chains without such structs are not touched.

The fallback only runs where the host aborted before. Generating the
marshaling code for these extensions would be the complete fix; the
table keeps up with vk.xml without regenerating the cereal modules.

Test: clang-cl /Zs of the six changed sources with the flags of the
      emulator build.
Test: a standalone check of the table: every field lies inside its
      struct, offsets ascend, sTypes are unique, the wire sizes of the
      acceleration structure and ray tracing pipeline properties (44
      and 32 bytes) and the 19 size_t fields of the descriptor buffer
      properties match the API 34 guest's reservedmarshal functions,
      and guest-shaped bytes survive a decode and re-encode.
